Q1. What is the Factory Method Design Pattern?
Why do we need it?

Interview Ready Answer

The Factory Method Pattern is a
Creational Design Pattern that
encapsulates object creation.

Instead of allowing the client to create
objects directly using the new keyword,

a Factory creates and returns
the required object.

------------------------------------------------------------

Why do we need Factory Method?

• Hides object creation logic.
• Reduces Tight Coupling.
• Improves Maintainability.
• Improves Scalability.
• Makes code easier to extend.
• Supports Open/Closed Principle.

------------------------------------------------------------

Difference from new Keyword

Without Factory

Car car = new Car();

The client directly knows
the concrete class.

------------------------------------------------------------

With Factory

Vehicle vehicle =
VehicleFactory.getVehicle("Car");

The client depends only on
the Vehicle interface.

The Factory decides
which object to create.

------------------------------------------------------------

Real-Life Example

Restaurant

Customer orders a Cold Drink.

The customer does not prepare it.

The Restaurant (Factory)
creates and serves the required drink.

------------------------------------------------------------

Software Industry Examples

• Spring BeanFactory
• JDBC DriverManager
• Logger Factory
• Notification Factory

