Q3. Difference between Singleton Pattern
and Factory Method Pattern

Interview Ready Answer

Singleton Pattern

• Ensures only one object exists.
• Returns the same object every time.
• Controls the number of objects.
• Uses
  - Private Constructor
  - Private Static Instance
  - Public Static getInstance()

Examples

• Logger
• Database Connection
• Configuration Manager

------------------------------------------------------------

Factory Method Pattern

• Creates objects based on requirement.
• May return different objects.
• Encapsulates object creation logic.
• Client doesn't know the
  concrete implementation.

Examples

• Vehicle Factory
• Notification Factory
• Spring BeanFactory

------------------------------------------------------------

Memory Trick

Singleton

↓

One Object

↓

Same Instance

----------------------------

Factory Method

↓

Many Objects

↓

Factory Decides

Which Object

