Trap 1

Question

What is the Factory Method Pattern?

Correct Answer

A Creational Design Pattern
that encapsulates object creation
and hides object creation logic
from the client.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 2

Question

Does Factory Method eliminate
the new keyword?

Correct Answer

No.

The new keyword is still used,

but inside the Factory,

not inside the client code.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 3

Question

What are the four main components
of Factory Method?

Correct Answer

• Product
• Concrete Products
• Factory
• Client

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 4

Question

Why is Factory Method better
than directly using new?

Correct Answer

• Reduces Tight Coupling.
• Centralizes Object Creation.
• Improves Maintainability.
• Improves Scalability.
• Supports Open/Closed Principle.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 5

Question

Can Factory Method return
different objects?

Correct Answer

Yes.

Depending on the client's request,

the Factory can return

Car

Bike

Truck

or any other implementation.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 6

Question

Can Singleton and Factory Method
be used together?

Correct Answer

Yes.

Example

A DatabaseConnectionFactory
can itself be implemented as
a Singleton,

ensuring only one Factory instance
creates database connections.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 7

Question

What is the biggest advantage
of Factory Method?

Correct Answer

The client depends on an
abstraction,

not on concrete classes.

This reduces Tight Coupling.

